pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* The version-2 spelling of
* `correct/version3/checked_deletion_witness_under_order.pbp`: a checked
* deletion may carry a witness while an order is loaded. Only the
* strengthening-to-core half of the format's "the substitution has to be empty"
* condition is real; under a loaded order `DeletionChecker` generates the
* order's proofgoals, so the witness has to not worsen the order rather than be
* absent. Both dialects reach the same code, and both are pinned because
* several past defects were reachable in only one of them.
f 2
pre_order simple
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end
load_order simple x1
* A derived constraint, so the acceptance below cannot be a silent fall back to
* unchecked deletion.
p 1 2 +
delc 1 ; x1 -> 0 x2 -> 1 ;
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
